==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*snewbʰ-||to marry, to wed}}. Possibly cognate with {{cog|grc|νύμφη||bride, young wife, nymph}} (English {{m|en|nymph}}), but this is disputed.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|nūbō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|nūbō|nūbere|nūpsī|nūptum|conj=3}}

# {{lb|la|transitive|rare}} I [[cover]], [[veil]].
# {{lb|la|intransitive|with dative}} I veil myself for, get married to, [[marry]], [[wed]] (for a woman).
## {{lb|la|intransitive|of plants}} I become joined, tied or [[wedded]] (to).

